{"name":"Spirit Mountain","hex":"#6a8b98","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spirit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soul of a person or other creature.","A supernatural being, often but not exclusively without physical form; ghost, fairy, angel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carry off, especially in haste, secrecy, or mystery.","Sometimes followed by up: to animate with vigour; to excite; to encourage; to inspirit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit"},{"term":"mountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevation of land of considerable dimensions rising more or less abruptly, forming a conspicuous figure in the landscape, usually having a small extent of surface at its summit. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something very large in size or quantity; a huge amount; a great heap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spirit Mountain (Montana)","blocks":[{"text":"Spirit Mountain is in the Beartooth Mountains in the U.S. state of Montana. The peak is one of the tallest in the Beartooth Mountains and is in the Absaroka-Beartooth Wilderness, in Custer National Forest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Spring_views_along_the_Beartooth_Highway_2021.jpg/330px-Spring_views_along_the_Beartooth_Highway_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_Mountain_(Montana)"},{"title":"Spirit Mountain (Nevada)","blocks":[{"text":"Spirit Mountain, also known as Avi Kwa Ame is a mountain within the Lake Mead National Recreation Area near Laughlin, Nevada. It is listed on the United States National Register of Historic Places as a sacred place to Native American tribes in Southern Nevada. Spirit Mountain is the highest point in the Spirit Mountain Wilderness and is the highest point in the Newberry Mountains with the summit peak at 5,639 feet (1,719 m)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spirit_Mountain_from_west_1.jpg/330px-Spirit_Mountain_from_west_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_Mountain_(Nevada)"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Beartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg/500px-Beartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Beartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg/1280px-Beartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Beartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg/500px-Beartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spirit Mountain from Beartooth Pass","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeartooth_Pass%2C_Spirit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Volc%C3%A1n_Chimborazo%2C_%22